      "properties": {
        "Node name for S&R": "Note"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "Camera pose -> 3D previews (three fidelity tiers)\n\nA real (here: synthetic) camera is calibrated from six chessboard views; one view's pose is recovered with solvePnP; 'CV Camera Pose To 3D View' adapts K + dist + rvec/tvec to a LOAD3D_CAMERA dict (board square = 1 scene unit; the milk truck stands in for the board at the origin). \n\n'CV Preview 3D (Calibrated Camera)' (this pack, web/cv_preview3d.js): projection built directly from K (off-axis cx/cy, fx != fy), pose INCLUDING roll, and the lens distortion (k1,k2,p1,p2,k3) replicated by an overscanned render + Brown-Conrady warp shader. With the pose photo as bg_image the truck composites onto the photographed board in register - toggle 'distortion' to see the lens model bend the render. Pick a gizmo mode (move/rotate/scale) and drag the truck: the placement lands in the object_transform widget, so re-running renders it (and its silhouette MASK) where you left it.\n\nSwap 'Calibrate Camera' for 'CV Load Camera Params (JSON)' to reuse a saved calibration - the bridge takes the same inputs. Failure-tolerant: on found=false, Solve PnP emits zero vectors and the bridge falls back to a frontal default view (no control flow needed).\n\nThe 3D model must sit in ComfyUI/input/3d/MilkTruck.glb (copy it from example_inputs/, see sources.txt)."
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
